/**
 * 512x512 blue-noise DITHER threshold texture (asset). NOT GENERATED HERE —
 * DOWNLOADED, on the user's instruction (2026-08-08): *"you don't generate blue
 * noise. you download it. there are git repos for blue noise to go"*.
 *
 * PROVENANCE: github.com/Calinou/free-blue-noise-textures, 512_512/LDR_LLL1_0.png
 * (the single-channel L variant), by Christoph Peters (2016-2017), published via
 * momentsingraphics.de. **LICENSE: CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain)** — no
 * attribution required, kept here because provenance is not the same as obligation.
 *
 * WHY IT REPLACED blue_noise_64.js, WHICH WAS NOT BLUE NOISE AT ALL. That tile's
 * docblock claimed Ulichney void-and-cluster with stated regeneration params; the
 * DATA matched none of it. Measured two independent ways after the user reported
 * "artifacts ... when emphasis = high and bit depth = 1" on a smooth gradient:
 *
 *   RANK PERMUTATION. Void-and-cluster ranks every texel, so an NxN tile holds
 *   EXACTLY N*N/256 of each value. Old 64x64: expected 16, measured min 8 / max 17
 *   -- never rank-ordered. This tile: expected 1024, measured min 1024 / max 1024.
 *
 *   LOW-FREQUENCY ENERGY, the property that IS blue noise. Variance of the field
 *   after a radius-3 box blur, as a percentage of a white-noise control's:
 *       old 64x64   279%   <-- MORE clumping than random
 *       this tile    11.6%
 *   A 2D DFT agrees: the old tile's high/low radial power ratio was 0.90 against a
 *   white-noise control's 1.03 -- a flat spectrum wearing a blue-noise label.
 *
 * That is the whole artifact. White (or worse) noise carries low-frequency energy,
 * so it CLUMPS; tiling a clumpy 64px tile across a frame repeats those clumps on a
 * 64px grid, and at 1 bit with high emphasis there is no headroom left to hide it.
 *
 * SIZE IS THE DELIBERATE TRADE, AND IT IS NOT SMALL: 262,144 raw bytes -> 349,528
 * base64 chars, versus the old tile's 5.5 KB. Random bytes do not gzip, so this is
 * a real ~262 KB of transfer. It buys two things at once -- a correct spectrum, and
 * a repeat period 8x longer (a 64px tile repeats ~30x17 times across 1080p; 512px
 * repeats ~4x2). The repo also ships 128_128 and 256_256 if that is judged too
 * expensive; DO NOT DOWNSAMPLE THIS ONE to get there, because resampling destroys
 * the spectrum that is the entire point -- take the repo's own tile at that size.
 *
 * Stored as base64 of 262144 single-byte gray THRESHOLD values (row-major, one byte
 * per texel; value/255 is the threshold in [0,1)). Consumed by
 * render_gpu/skia/dither_shader.js, which expands it to an RGBA CanvasKit Image.
 */

/** The blue-noise tile edge length in texels. */
export const BLUE_NOISE_SIZE = 512;

/** Base64 of the 262144 row-major 8-bit threshold values. */
export const BLUE_NOISE_BASE64 =
  "";

const B64 = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/";

/**
 * Pure function. Decodes a base64 string to a Uint8Array. Self-contained (no
 * atob/Buffer) so it runs identically in the browser and in Node.
 *
 * @param {string} b64 - base64 text (standard alphabet, optional '=' padding)
 * @returns {Uint8Array} the decoded bytes
 *
 * @example decodeBase64("QUJD") // Uint8Array [65, 66, 67]  ("ABC")
 */
export function decodeBase64(b64) {
  const clean = b64.replace(/=+$/, "");
  const out = new Uint8Array((clean.length * 3) >> 2);
  let acc = 0, bits = 0, oi = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < clean.length; i++) {
    const v = B64.indexOf(clean[i]);
    if (v < 0) throw new Error("decodeBase64: non-base64 character in input");
    acc = (acc << 6) | v;
    bits += 6;
    if (bits >= 8) { bits -= 8; out[oi++] = (acc >> bits) & 0xff; }
  }
  return out;
}

/**
 * Pure function. The decoded blue-noise threshold tile (row-major), one byte per
 * texel: BLUE_NOISE_SIZE² = 262144 bytes at the shipped 512x512.
 *
 * @returns {Uint8Array} length BLUE_NOISE_SIZE² (262144 at 512x512), each byte a threshold
 *
 * @example decodeBlueNoise().length // 262144
 */
export function decodeBlueNoise() {
  const bytes = decodeBase64(BLUE_NOISE_BASE64);
  if (bytes.length !== BLUE_NOISE_SIZE * BLUE_NOISE_SIZE)
    throw new Error(`decodeBlueNoise: expected ${BLUE_NOISE_SIZE * BLUE_NOISE_SIZE} bytes, got ${bytes.length}`);
  return bytes;
}
